meta {
  name: Create Asset
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/assets
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "url": "https://picsum.photos/id/237/300/300.jpg",
    "filename": "wc_test_asset.jpg",
    "alt_text": "WC test asset",
    "category_ids": ["6a9f1b862b6fd055ffb7c7de"]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.content_type: eq image/jpeg
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". **Fixture
  kept** -- id `6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f`, for Products (Phase 2b)'s
  `thumbnail_id`.

  `201 Created`. Plytix downloaded the public image from `url` and stored
  it (`content_type`, `checksum`, `extension`, `file_size` all populated
  from the real file).

  ## Major finding -- category_ids is silently ignored on create
  `category_ids` was sent with a real category id (Phase 1b's fixture)
  but **does not link** -- a follow-up `GET /assets/{id}/categories`
  right after this create returns `[]`. The linkage only takes effect via
  a separate `PATCH` after creation -- see "Update Asset.bru" in this
  folder, which sets `category_ids` again and confirms it actually
  applies that time. **This is resource-specific**: the same
  `category_ids` field on `POST /products` (Phase 2b) *does* link at
  create time -- don't assume this behavior generalizes across resources
  either way; test per-resource.

  ## Required fields -- cross-field rule not in spec (absorbed from "Create Asset - Empty Body (422).bru")
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08. `AssetCreateInputDto` marks **no** fields
  required in `openapi_pimv3.json` (`url`, `content`, `filename`,
  `alt_text`, `category_ids`, `static_list_ids` all optional) -- but the
  live API still enforces a real cross-field rule not expressible in the
  schema's `required` list: either `url` or `content` must be provided.
  Empty body returns 422 with `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":
  "InputDTOValidationError","description":"Value error, Either 'url' or
  'content' must be provided"}]}`.

  ## GET by ID response shape (confirmed live 2026-09-21)
  Real fixture `6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b187a`:
  `{"id":"6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b187a","account_id":"6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
  "assigned":true,"content_type":"image/jpeg",
  "checksum":"13b0321c87707fe209f075e73a0f8cec75112c3690d3ab4544866e5ad0662230",
  "extension":"jpg","file_size":229898,"file_type":"IMAGES",
  "file_modified":"2025-04-01T16:27:25.911000",
  "filename":"VST-59102_4.jpg",
  "path":"public_files/pim/assets/a5/f5/38/6a/6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c/images/d8/f5/38/6a/6a38f5d8c3d65a5f868b187a/VST-59102_4.jpg",
  "n_catalogs":0,"n_products":4,"status":"ACTIVE",
  "created":"2026-06-22T08:44:10","modified":"2026-06-22T08:44:10.020000"}`.
}

example {
  name: Empty Body (422)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08. Either url or content is required even though both are marked optional in the spec.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/assets
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {}
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "Value error, Either 'url' or 'content' must be provided"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
